**What was created:**

`internal/config/watch.go` — `Watch(ctx, log)` watches the **directory** containing the config file (not the file itself) so rename-based editor saves work. A single goroutine runs the event loop: filesystem events for other files are filtered by basename, each matching event resets a 500ms debounce timer, and when the timer fires it calls `Load()`. Valid configs are sent non-blocking on a buffered channel (size 1); invalid configs are logged and dropped. The goroutine exits and closes the channel when `ctx` is cancelled.

`internal/config/watch_test.go` — five tests covering: successful reload, invalid config rejection (validation failure, nothing emitted), debounce (3 rapid writes → 1 reload), context cancellation (channel closed), and write-rename editor pattern (atomic rename detected via directory watch).
